---
import PageHero from "../components/PageHero.astro";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { fullAddress, site } from "../data/site";
// Plain-language policy that matches what the site does today. Have it reviewed before launch.
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Trivista Labs"
  description="How Trivista Labs handles the information you send through this website."
>
  <PageHero eyebrow="Legal" title="Privacy Policy" scene={false}>
    <p class="mono-label">Last updated <time datetime={site.privacyUpdated.iso}>{site.privacyUpdated.display}</time></p>
  </PageHero>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          This policy explains what information {site.legalName} (&ldquo;Trivista Labs&rdquo;, &ldquo;we&rdquo;)
          collects through trivistalabs.io, and how we use it.
        </p>

        <h2>What we collect</h2>
        <p>Through the contact form, we collect what you choose to send us:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>your name and email address</li>
          <li>your company name, if you give it</li>
          <li>the type of project and the timeline you choose</li>
          <li>your message</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          If you apply for a role, you send your CV and any links by email to
          <a href={`mailto:${site.careersEmail}`}>{site.careersEmail}</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>How we use it</h2>
        <p>
          We use your details only to reply to your enquiry and to discuss the project you asked about, and a CV only to
          consider you for a role at Trivista Labs. We do not sell your information or share it with anyone for
          marketing.
        </p>

        <h2>Analytics and cookies</h2>
        <p>
          We use Google Analytics to understand how this website is used: which pages are visited, how visitors arrive,
          roughly where they are (country and city, worked out from the IP address), the device and browser they use,
          and which buttons they click, such as &ldquo;Start a project&rdquo;. Google Analytics does not see what you
          write in the contact form.
        </p>
        <p>
          Outside the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom and Switzerland, Google Analytics sets cookies, named
          <code>_ga</code>, to recognise a returning browser. Inside those areas it sets no analytics cookies, and visits
          are counted without them. Advertising features are switched off everywhere, and we do not use analytics to
          identify you.
        </p>
        <p>
          Google handles this data under its own <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">privacy policy</a>. You
          can stop Google Analytics measuring your visits with Google&rsquo;s
          <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout">opt-out browser add-on</a>, or by blocking cookies in your
          browser.
        </p>

        <h2>How it is handled</h2>
        <p>
          When you send the form, your message goes to our server, which is hosted by Render, and is delivered to our
          team’s inbox by email through Resend. This website is hosted on GitHub Pages. Like most hosting providers,
          these services may keep technical logs, such as IP addresses, to run and protect their systems.
        </p>

        <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
        <p>
          We keep enquiry emails for as long as we need them to respond to you and to keep a record of our business
          conversations. You can ask us to delete them at any time.
        </p>

        <h2>Your choices</h2>
        <p>
          You can ask us to show you, correct or delete the personal information we hold about you. Email
          <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> and we will respond as soon as we can.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>If we change how we handle information, we will update this page and the date at the top.</p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          {site.legalName}, {fullAddress}. Email: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
